loom qa itinerary=A composite=94 shelf=A+ composite=99
file construction/ITINERARY.md the heading names what stands under it; three landed rows to the shelf; 1,352 bytes of headroom where there were 14
file construction/archive/20260831-023122_itinerary-settled-decisions.md the third shelf -- three landed rows held word for word, with the test the card's own law names
file construction/CHECKPOINTS.md the walk-back row, written before the condense, its byte figure measured rather than estimated
file session-logs/date/README-index-20260831.md this lap's row
recommend keep-going -- THE ROUND THAT WAS LOST TWICE IS LANDED, and the lesson it cost two laps to teach is written where the next hand reads it: the stash preserves work, and only a commit ends a lap. THE FINDING WORTH CARRYING is that the card's heading had gone false by accretion -- eleven blocks under a name for one -- which no byte bound and no link guard can see, because both read what is there rather than whether the sign over it still tells the truth. MINE NEXT: the card's remaining recording blocks, which this pass halved rather than finished, and %360's own remainder now stands closed in this lane. YOUR GATES ARE WHERE THEY WERE: rule_twin at %7, gate %5 on the Pond switchover, and %374's receipt-chain question, which is why this lap had to choose between a full pass and a landed round at all.
